<h1>deterministic finite automata string search</h1>
<p>
(algorithm)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A <a href="stringMatching.html"><em>string matching</em></a> algorithm which builds a <a href="determFinitStateMach.html"><em>deterministic finite state machine</em></a> to recognize the search string.  The machine is then run at each location in turn.  If the machine accepts, that is a match.
</p>


<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>
<h2>Implementation</h2>
<a href="http://www-igm.univ-mlv.fr/~lecroq/string/node4.html" target="_blank">description and animation (C)</a>, <a href="https://users.dcc.uchile.cl/~rbaeza/handbook/algs/7/716.srch.c" target="_blank">(C)</a> which uses a <a href="https://users.dcc.uchile.cl/~rbaeza/handbook/algs/7/716.def.c" target="_blank">finite automaton structure (C)</a> and <a href="https://users.dcc.uchile.cl/~rbaeza/handbook/algs/7/716.straut.c" target="_blank">builds a recognizer (C)</a>

<hr>

Go to the
<a href="https://www.nist.gov/dads/">Dictionary of Algorithms and Data
Structures</a> home page.

